    <section class="section" id="how-it-works">
<h1>How <span>NOTIFY</span> works from Moodle to your phone</h1>

    <p>
      NOTIFY is intended to help students keep up with academic activity on Moodle.
      This guide explains how a student accesses the service, what the homepage
      sections are for, and how new Moodle information is expected to become a
      phone notification.
    </p>
 <div>
          <h2>Accessing a NOTIFY account</h2>

          <p class="section-subtitle">
            Students use a NOTIFY account to manage the service and connect
            their Moodle account.
          </p>
 <article class="info-card">

          <div class="icon">LOGIN</div>

          <h3>For a student who already has an account</h3>

          <p>
            The student opens the NOTIFY website and selects <strong>Log In</strong>.
            They enter the email address and password they used when registering
            for NOTIFY. After the details have been checked successfully, the
            student is taken to their account homepage, where they can view
            their notification settings and the Moodle account connected
            to their profile.
          </p>

<div class="icon">SIGN UP</div>

          <h3>For a student who does not have an account</h3>

          <p>
            The student selects <strong>Sign Up</strong> on the NOTIFY website
            and completes the registration details requested by the service,
            such as their name and email address. They create a password and
            complete any required email verification. Once registration is
            complete, they can use the new email address and password to log
            in to NOTIFY and continue with the Moodle connection process.
          </p>



        </article>



      <p class="note">
        <strong>Information:</strong>
        A NOTIFY account is separate from a Moodle account. A real version
        should never ask students to share their Moodle password directly
        with an untrusted service; the Moodle connection should use an
        approved, secure authorization method.
      </p>





        </div>

